       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The reason given, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose twice the maximum. At 6,400 mg/day, the risk of serious harm is high. That includes GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum). This may be the closest option to what you want.\n- **Enter a different regimen** that you choose within labeled limits.\n- **Help with a different analgesic or an adjunct**, such as scheduled acetaminophen, if pain control is the goal. I'd need you to specify the drug and dose.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the maximum dose, please talk to the pharmacy or the attending first. Then the order can go through the normal override process. Tell me which of the options above you want and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
